1
00:05:26,666 --> 00:05:32,666
A remarkable true story of human space exploration

2
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:59,333
Searching for Skylab, America's Forgotten Triumph is a documentary,
history, family film directed by Dwight Steven-Boniecki.

3
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:26,000
The first American space station Skylab is found in
pieces scattered in Western Australia.

4
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:52,666
Putting these pieces back together and re-tracing the Skylab program back to its
very conception reveals the cornerstone of human space exploration.

5
00:27:13,333 --> 00:27:19,333
Self - Skylab-2 Scientist Pilot (NASA Astronaut),
played by Joseph P. (Joe) Kerwin.

6
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Self - Skylab-2 Pilot (NASA Astronaut), played by Paul J. Weitz.

7
00:38:06,666 --> 00:38:12,666
Self - Skylab-3 Pilot (NASA Astronaut), played by Jack R. Lousma.

8
00:43:33,333 --> 00:43:39,333
Self - Skylab-3 Scientist Pilot (NASA Astronaut), played by Owen Garriott.

9
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Self - Skylab-4 Commander (NASA Astronaut), played by Gerald P. (Jerry) Carr.

10
00:54:26,666 --> 00:54:32,666
Self - Skylab-4 Scientist Pilot (NASA Astronaut),
played by Edward George Gibson.

11
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:59,333
Searching for Skylab - America's Forgotten Triumph is a 2019
documentary about the 1970s American space station Skylab.

12
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
It was written by Carl Alessi and directed by Dwight
Steven-Boniecki and partly crowdfunded.

13
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
Searching for Skylab was created to bring attention to the important role
Skylab played in the development of human spaceflight programs.

14
01:16:13,333 --> 01:16:19,333
Of Skylab, Steven-Boniecki said, "Hundreds of hours of video and audio recordings exist from it, yet it is unlikely that you've seen or heard much of it."
A preview of the first
working version of Searching for Skylab was screened at Spacefest, in Tucson, Arizona, July 5, 2018 to a crowd of space experts, astronauts and their families.

15
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
In November 2018, shortly before the film's completion, a sneak peek of the movie’s working
version was presented at the Science Late Show at the Kosmos Kino in Zürich.

16
01:27:06,666 --> 01:27:12,666
The finished documentary was released February 8, 2019, the 45th
anniversary of the splashdown of the last Skylab crew.

17
01:32:33,333 --> 01:32:39,333
The film explores themes of hero, nasa, space suit, space travel, space mission.
